# klip-dictionary-data v3 — provenance manifest
#
# Every number in a REBUILT block is measured, not carried over. One block per
# language.
#
# v3 REBUILDS THREE LANGUAGES ONLY: zh, ja, ko. The Han single-character
# rescue (Klip PR #257) changed the entry classifier, and it can only move
# rows in a Han-script language. The other SIXTEEN blocks are CARRIED OVER
# FROM v2 VERBATIM -- every measured field is the v2 figure, byte for byte,
# because those assets are the v2 artifacts unchanged and were not rebuilt.
# Each such block says so on its `status` line, which is the ONLY line added
# to it.
#
# THE SIXTEEN CARRIED ASSETS ARE NOT ATTACHED TO THIS RELEASE. v3 attaches
# FIVE files: the three rebuilt .jsonl.gz, export_pack.py, and this manifest.
# To obtain any of the other sixteen, fetch it from the v2 release -- the
# asset.sha256 recorded in its block below is the hash of THAT file, and is
# how you confirm you have the right one. A block in this manifest is a
# PROVENANCE RECORD for the dataset, not a claim that the file sits in this
# release's asset list.
#
# BUILDER      Klip commit cb49b835d38567f8a8d3ffd284f414041e6ad513 (develop,
#              the #257 merge), tool/dict_pack/build_pack.dart
#              -- applies to the THREE REBUILT BLOCKS.
#              The sixteen carried blocks were built at
#              09a912748412d2b09681390a7103b21150974a8a (the #256 merge),
#              which is what their numbers measure. A block's builder is the
#              commit named on its own status line, never this one by default.
# EXPORTER     export_pack.py in this repo, python3 -I, stdlib only.
#              A column-to-key dump of the pack. No filtering, no reshaping.
#              UNCHANGED from v2 and re-attached byte-identical.
# CHAIN        kaikki extract -> Dart pack (.sqlite) -> gzipped JSONL asset
#              Each link is hashed below so any link can be re-verified.
#
# THE THREE EXTRACTS WERE RE-VERIFIED BEFORE THE v3 BUILD, not assumed: each
# extract.sha256 below was recomputed from the file in ~/dict-work/ and
# matched the value v2 recorded. The inputs are therefore pinned across both
# releases, so the entry-count deltas are attributable to the classifier
# change alone and to nothing in the source.
#
# WHY THE EXTRACT HASH IS HERE AND WAS NOT IN v1: kaikki.org serves a ROLLING
# dump with no versioned archive. v1 recorded no extract hash, so v1's numbers
# are not reproducible -- the gender fix's removal count came out 2,806 against
# one snapshot and 2,828 against another, a gap that can no longer be closed.
# v2 pins every input, and v3 re-verified those pins.
#
# THE PACKS ARE INTERMEDIATES AND WERE DELETED AFTER EXPORT. They are not
# published. Each is reproducible from the extract hashed below plus the
# builder commit for that block, and its hash is recorded here so a rebuild
# can be checked against what actually produced these assets.
#
